 "_comment": [
  "THE shared Rust <-> TypeScript number/date text corpus (P2 S1, app locale everywhere).",
  "Read by core/engine/src/locale_corpus_tests.rs AND app/src/core/lib/locale/__tests__/localeText.corpus.test.ts.",
  "op: format = number_format::format_number(General) or custom_format::format_custom_value(code);",
  "    parse = typed_entry::parse_number (null = refused); parseDate = typed_entry::parse_date_time_input serial (null = refused);",
  "    formatDate = the locale's short | long | time | dateTime pattern (dateTime = date_format + ' ' + time_format).",
  "Format CODES are invariant (en-US syntax). Grouping in sv-SE/fr-FR is U+00A0. Numbers compare within 1e-9.",
  "locales: each locale exactly as get_locale_settings sends it (LocaleSettingsData, camelCase), so the TypeScript suite",
  "    formats with the very settings Rust uses; locale_corpus_tests.rs pins every entry to LocaleSettings::from_locale_id + calendar()."
 ],
